# Copy to ops/alerts.env and fill in. That copy is gitignored.
#
# ## Getting the two values
#
# The token: message @BotFather on Telegram, /newbot, and it hands you one.
# It looks like 123456789:AAH... and it is a password — anyone holding it can
# post as your bot. It is read by ops/alerts.ts and used in exactly one place,
# the request URL; it is never logged, never written to the state file and
# never put in a message. ops/check-alerts.mjs enforces that.
#
# The chat id: send your new bot any message, then open
#   https://api.telegram.org/bot<token>/getUpdates
# and read `message.chat.id` out of the reply. A bot cannot start a
# conversation, which is why you have to speak first.
export WARDA_TELEGRAM_TOKEN=""
export WARDA_TELEGRAM_CHAT=""

# ## Console accounts (optional)
#
# The site runs every console account's alert rules when asked; this asks it
# every 15 minutes (ops/console-alerts.sh, installed by ops/install-cron.sh).
# CONSOLE_CRON_SECRET is the same value as CRON_SECRET in the Vercel project.
export CONSOLE_URL="https://www.wardaprotocol.com"
export CONSOLE_CRON_SECRET=""
